ICCV-2023-P0932,ICCV-2023-A004930,Liliane Momeni,shared,3,5,5,"Verb phrase loss Negative captions in the batch Hard negative loss Figure . Verb-Focused Contrastive (VFC) learning: (Left): Given a video and its corresponding caption, we leverage a Large Language Model (LLM) to output ( ) hard negative captions, where only the verb has been changed while keeping the remaining context, and ( ) verb phrases which succinctly describe the action in the video. (Right): To encourage better verb reasoning, we subsequently enforce ( ) a calibrated hard negative loss, using our generated hard negative captions and other captions in the batch, and ( ) a fine-grained, verb phrase loss. We show that VFC improves verb understanding of video-language models compared to the standard contrastive loss.",-4,data/raw/iccv/2023/first_pages/ICCV-2023-P0932.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2023/papers/Momeni_Verbs_in_Action_Improving_Verb_Understanding_in_Video-Language_Models_ICCV_2023_paper.pdf
