ICCV-2023-P1428,ICCV-2023-A007564,Jianglong Ye,shared,3,3,3,"UC San Diego TuSimple Input Rendered Feature Map 2D Keypoints Transfer 3D Keypoints Transfer 2D Part Co-segmentation (a) 3D Part Co-segmentation (b) Figure : While most generalizable NeRFs focus on novel-view synthesis, we propose a framework named FeatureNeRF to learn 3D semantic representations by distilling vision foundation models. After distillation, FeatureNeRF allows to render novel-view feature maps given a single input image (a), which can be leveraged to various downstream tasks. Here, we show how we propagate part segmentation labels and keypoints to different views and instances in both 2D and 3D domains (b).",-4,data/raw/iccv/2023/first_pages/ICCV-2023-P1428.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2023/papers/Ye_FeatureNeRF_Learning_Generalizable_NeRFs_by_Distilling_Foundation_Models_ICCV_2023_paper.pdf
