ICCV-2023-P1702,ICCV-2023-A009070,Balamurugan Thambiraja,shared,3,6,6,"Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems, Tübingen, Germany Max Planck Institute for Informatics, Saarland, Germany Mesh Labs, Microsoft, Cambridge, UK Figure : Imitator is a novel method for personalized speech-driven 3D facial animation. Given an audio sequence and a personalized style-embedding as input, we generate person-specific motion sequences with accurate lip closures for bilabial consonants (’m’,’b’,’p’). The style-embedding of a subject can be computed from a short reference video (e.g., 5s).",2,data/raw/iccv/2023/first_pages/ICCV-2023-P1702.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2023/papers/Thambiraja_Imitator_Personalized_Speech-driven_3D_Facial_Animation_ICCV_2023_paper.pdf
