s including eight major types of cancers and occurring non-cancer tumors (all are pathology-confirmed with 3D tumor masks annotated by radiologists). On the test set of patients, CancerUniT has demonstrated strong performance under a set of clinically relevant evaluation metrics, substantially outperforming both multi-disease methods and an assembly of eight single-organ expert models in tumor detection, Tumor Segmentation & Diagnosis Cancer Detection in Organs",-9,data/raw/iccv/2023/first_pages/ICCV-2023-P1865.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2023/papers/Chen_CancerUniT_Towards_a_Single_Unified_Model_for_Effective_Detection_Segmentation_ICCV_2023_paper.pdf
